Subject: [qnx-porter 0002] add-include
Source: deterministic rule
Reason: `ntohl` is a macro in QNX's <arpa/inet.h>, and neither libc nor libsocket exports it as a function. apps/db_dump/db_dump.c did not include the header, so the compiler took it for an undeclared function, and the link failed.
Error: /home/chirag/qnx-porter/ports/mosquitto/work/src/apps/db_dump/db_dump.c:507:(.text.startup+0x504): undefined reference to `ntohl'
---
diff --git a/apps/db_dump/db_dump.c b/apps/db_dump/db_dump.c
index 9cf48c8..61c82b7 100644
--- a/apps/db_dump/db_dump.c
+++ b/apps/db_dump/db_dump.c
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ Contributors:
 #include <uthash.h>
 
 #include "db_dump.h"
+#include <arpa/inet.h>  /* qnx-porter: needed on QNX */
 
 #ifdef __ANDROID__
 #include <sys/endian.h>
